    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.metadata-vocabularies",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Resource Metadata Extensions, line 144: r3_vocabularies keys MUST be vocabulary URIs, urn:aauth:vocabulary: ones for the standard vocabularies",
      "anchor": "resource-metadata-extensions",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.token-claims",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Resource Token Extensions, lines 497-503: a Resource token carrying R3 information MUST include both r3_uri and r3_s256 (also checked: Resource iss, and aud naming the AS in four-party or the PS in three-party access, line 499)",
      "anchor": "resource-token-extensions",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.document-signature",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "R3 Document, line 448: the Resource MUST require a valid HTTP Message Signature on requests to R3 document URIs and MUST reject requests not signed by the entitled AS or PS; agents cannot fetch R3 documents",
      "anchor": "r3-document",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.document-entitlement",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "R3 Document Access Restriction, lines 729-734: the Resource MUST reject any signer, identified by id, that is not the AS in the Resource token's aud or the PS in its ps; any other signer MUST be rejected",
      "anchor": "r3-document-access-restriction",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.content-addressing",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Content Addressing, lines 486-488: r3_s256 is the SHA-256 of the bytes as served; the Resource MUST serve those exact bytes on every request for the same r3_uri, here to each entitled signer",
      "anchor": "content-addressing",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.document-fields",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Fields, lines 469-471: vocabulary is REQUIRED and MUST match a vocabulary advertised in r3_vocabularies; operations is REQUIRED",
      "anchor": "fields",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.composition",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Operations Spanning Multiple Definitions, line 435: the Resource MUST reference a single R3 document that covers all of the requested operations",
      "anchor": "operations-spanning-definitions",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.operation-validation",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Operation Validation, line 748: the Resource MUST validate declared operations against its authoritative definition before issuing a Resource token; an operation outside it, or a vocabulary the Resource does not advertise (line 412), gets no Resource token",
      "anchor": "operation-validation",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.grant-enforcement",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Grant Enforcement, line 758: Resources MUST enforce r3_granted and r3_per_call and MUST reject API calls that match an operation in neither claim",
      "anchor": "grant-enforcement",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.granted-served",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Resource Enforcement, step 1 (line 625): a call matching r3_granted is served; the 2xx status and the operation echo are the launcher's",
      "anchor": "resource-enforcement",
      "scope": "adapter-contract"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.document-signature-error",
      "source": "core",
      "section": "Verification (Server), lines 2242-2250, applied to the R3 document endpoint: any failure MUST result in a 401 with the appropriate Signature-Error; missing signature fields (step 1) and a signature that does not verify (step 7) are invalid_signature",
      "anchor": "verification",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.per-call-requirement",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Grant Enforcement, line 758: operations in r3_per_call MUST trigger an AAuth-Requirement before being served; the challenge is a 401 or 202 whose Resource token references a proposal, not the class document, names the AS in aud and the presented Auth token in presented_jti (Flow, step 1, line 675; line 499)",
      "anchor": "grant-enforcement",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.proposal-fields",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Proposal Document, lines 643-645: a per-call proposal's operations (REQUIRED) is the single r3_per_call operation invoked and its parameters (REQUIRED) carry the call's concrete parameters; it is content-addressed like a class document (line 637)",
      "anchor": "proposal-document",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.per-call-parameters",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Flow, step 3, line 677: on the 401 retry the Resource MUST verify the presented parameters match the approved proposal and MUST reject the call if anything differs; nothing is executed",
      "anchor": "per-call-flow",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.resource",
      "id": "r3.resource.per-call-single-use",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Flow, step 4, line 678: a Resource MUST NOT execute more than one invocation under one per-call Auth token; the launcher counts its own executions",
      "anchor": "per-call-flow",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.issuer",
      "id": "r3.issuer.fetch",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Issuer Processing, lines 543-546: an issuer receiving a Resource token carrying r3_uri and r3_s256 MUST fetch the R3 document at r3_uri",
      "anchor": "issuer-processing",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.issuer",
      "id": "r3.issuer.fetch-signature",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "R3 Document Access Restriction, line 729: a party fetching r3_uri MUST sign the request as a server in its own right, under the jwks_uri scheme with id set to its issuer (aauth-person.json for a PS)",
      "anchor": "r3-document-access-restriction",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.issuer",
      "id": "r3.issuer.hash-mismatch",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Issuer Processing, step 3, line 547: if the SHA-256 of the bytes received does not match r3_s256, the issuer MUST reject the Resource token",
      "anchor": "issuer-processing",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.issuer",
      "id": "r3.issuer.hash-verification",
      "source": "r3",
      "section": "Hash Verification, line 740: a party that fetches an R3 document MUST verify r3_s256 against it before using it; with no document fetched there is nothing verified to grant from",
      "anchor": "hash-verification",
      "scope": "protocol"
    },
    {
      "role": "r3.issuer",
      "id": "r3.issuer.auth-claims",
      "source": "r3",
